# FutureFeatureOverlay (v2 features)

Use `components/FutureFeatureOverlay.tsx` for features deferred to v2. Do **not** hide UI—slightly dim children, add a scrim that **darkens on hover and press**, and show the dark pill badge **"Coming Soon"** (with small `v2` tag). Children stay `pointer-events-none`; the wrapper receives hover.

```tsx
import FutureFeatureOverlay from '@/components/FutureFeatureOverlay';

<FutureFeatureOverlay>
  {/* section to mark */}
</FutureFeatureOverlay>
```

Optional: `className` on the wrapper (e.g. `min-h-[480px]` for full pages), `badgeClassName` for badge positioning on dark backgrounds.

## Currently marked v2

| Area | Target |
|------|--------|
| Individual | Fragmentation Index `MetricCard` |
| Manager | `OrgPulse`; "What's worth a conversation" (label + card); Team table KPI Progress column (`TeamTable futureFeatureKpiColumn`) |
| Executive | Context Savings `BigMetric` |
| Insights | Entire page content |
| Benchmarks | Entire page content |

## Adding new v2 sections

- Wrap with `FutureFeatureOverlay` unless only one table column needs marking—then use column-level dim + badge (see `TeamTable`).
- Keep interactive v1 areas **outside** the overlay when only part of a page is v2.
- Do not remove or restructure wrapped sections; overlay is additive only.
